    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5926": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I - Lecturer - Family and Consumer Sciences - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I - Lecturer - Family and Consumer Sciences - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I - Lecturer - Family and Consumer Sciences - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Educ & Human Dvlpmt Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Family & Consumer Sciences Posting Detail Information Posting Number F354P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade FS1 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Main Campus Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Generous benefit package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary The Department of Family and Consumer Sciences at Western Michigan University invites applications for a Faculty Specialist I in Workforce Education. This is a unique opportunity to prepare the next generation of Career and Technical Education teachers and workforce development professionals at a time when demand for both has never been higher. The successful candidate will teach across undergraduate and graduate programs in Business Education, Family and Consumer Sciences, and Industrial Technology Education, while coordinating the program’s intern teacher internship experience. This role is ideal for an experienced educator who wants to shape future CTE teachers and training professionals while staying connected to the classroom. Major Duties Teach core undergraduate and graduate courses in Workforce Education, including career and employability skills, student assessment, curriculum development, and teaching methods. Coordinate and run the program’s intern teacher internship, including placing candidates in school settings, building relationships with cooperating teachers and school partners, and conducting site visits. Evaluate intern performance and ensure candidates meet Michigan Department of Education certification requirements. Advise and mentor students across five undergraduate majors and the Workforce Education graduate program. Support students preparing for careers as CTE teachers, workplace trainers, and workforce development specialists. Participate in departmental, college, and university service. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in Career and Technical Education, Workforce Education, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Teaching experience in a relevant CTE discipline (Business Education, Family and Consumer Sciences, or Industrial Technology Education). Experience with student teacher supervision, mentoring, or internship coordination. Strong communication and relationship-building skills for working with school partners and cooperating teachers. Desired Qualifications Experience teaching at the college or university level. Familiarity with Michigan teacher certification requirements and processes. Background in workforce development or corporate training settings. Established relationships with regional schools or industry training partners. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Position Information Visit wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Other Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
