    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5857": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer - Mathematics - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer - Mathematics - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer - Mathematics - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload the required leadership statement as other. Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Arts And Sciences Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Mathematics Posting Detail Information Posting Number F349P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade FS1/FS2 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Main Campus Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Generous benefit package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary The Department of Mathematics at Western Michigan University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the Faculty Specialist I or II rank in Mathematics. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the teaching and service missions of WMU . This is an academic-year position, with the possibility of summer instructional assignments for additional compensation. The expected start date is August 15, 2027. Major Duties Provide effective mathematics instruction to undergraduate students in service courses. Support the success of the diverse populations of undergraduate students, including adjusting offerings for the changing backgrounds of students and the needs of client disciplines. Lead teams of instructors (including graduate students and adjunct instructors) in multi-section courses, including schedule, syllabus, course objectives, assessments, and professional development. Contribute to department, college, and university committees. Minimum Qualifications A master’s or doctoral degree in applied mathematics, mathematics, mathematics education, or a closely related field, awarded by August 15, 2028 from an accredited institution. Three years undergraduate teaching in mathematics or a closely related field. Experience working with multiple instructors on a common course. Experience with online learning-management systems. Desired Qualifications Evidence of successful and innovative mathematics teaching. Established capacity to serve as lead coordinator for multi-section courses. This includes providing course-specific professional development, mentoring and supervision for new instructors. Demonstrated ability to teach classes that provide technical skills for students enrolled in non- STEM majors, such as MATH 1140 and 1160 at WMU . Demonstrated ability to teach classes that improve the pre-algebra and algebra skills of students to prepare them for the math courses and content required for their majors and careers ( MATH 1090, 1100, and 1110 at WMU ). Ability to serve as support or lead the coordination of other multi-section courses if the need arises, including precalculus, calculus sequence, and linear algebra ( MATH 1178, 1179, 1180, 1220, 1230, 2300, 2720, 3740) or mathematics education ( MATH 1520, 2530, 2530, and 3550). A documented history of promoting student engagement, success, and achievement. An exhibited ability to implement AI or other technologies in the classroom. Special Instructions to Applicants Please upload the required leadership statement as other. Additional Position Information Go to: wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Teaching Philosophy Samples of Teaching Materials Transcripts Other Optional Documents Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
