    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5736": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I - Clinical Specialist - Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I - Clinical Specialist - Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I - Clinical Specialist - Speech, Language, Hearing Sciences - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Health & Human Svcs Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Speech,Language,Hearing Sci Posting Detail Information Posting Number F345P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade FS1 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - East Campus Salary Range Pay is commensurate with qualifications and experience, combined with an excellent benefits package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary Western Michigan University invites applications for the position of Clinical Faculty Specialist I. This is a tenure-track, full-time, fiscal year position. The University: Western Michigan University ( WMU ), located in Southwest Michigan, is a vibrant, nationally recognized student-centered research institution with an enrollment of over 18,000. WMU delivers high-quality undergraduate instruction, has a strong graduate division, and fosters significant research activities. The Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching classifies WMU as a doctoral university and one of just 185 public universities in the nation conducting research at a high level. The College: In 1976, pioneering allied health and human services professional programs united in the WMU College of Health and Human Services, carrying on a tradition of excellence and innovation that began in 1922 with the establishment of the occupational therapy program. That tradition continues today. The College of Health and Human Services has high-quality, nationally ranked academic programs; exceptional students and faculty; unmatched clinical education; many regular opportunities for inter-professional education; state-of-the-art teaching facilities; outreach, service and community engagement; and a strong research record that is helping shape the future of health care. The college is composed of departments, schools, centers and clinics. Departments include Blindness and Low Vision Studies; Occupational Therapy; Physical Therapy; Physician Assistant; and Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences. The college’s schools include Interdisciplinary Health Programs, with programs in Gerontology, Healthcare Administration, Integrative Holistic Health and Wellness, Healthcare Services and Sciences, and Public Health; Nursing; and Social Work. The college also houses the Ph.D. in Interdisciplinary Health Sciences Program. The college also operates the Center for Disability Services, Aging Services, the Resiliency Center for Families and Children, and the Unified Clinics, a multidisciplinary service/training clinic. CHHS is housed on east campus in Kalamazoo, Michigan, with online and regional programs that extend the depth and breadth of the college’s access and influence. Approximately 100 board appointed faculty serve approximately 1,202 undergraduate and 715 graduate students, with majors and programs that lead to bachelor’s, master’s and doctoral degrees. A number of graduate certificate programs and undergraduate minors are also offered. The students and faculty of the College of Health and Human Services extend the energy of the college and University through significant efforts toward community engagement and service. With required internships, field placements and clinical rotations alone, faculty-supervised CHHS students provide more than 600,000 hours of service annually to children and families in the community, region and across the nation. Substantial volunteerism increases this positive impact. The mission of the College of Health and Human Services is to engage every person in an experiential, interprofessional and inclusive academic environment that inspires compassion, integrity and advocacy. We prepare all learners to thrive in health and human services careers that are high in demand, high in purpose, high in satisfaction and unsurpassed in impact. Department: The Department of Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences enrolls approximately 60 students in the two-year M.A. program in speech-language pathology, 130 in the undergraduate major, and supports a minor in American Sign Language. Department of Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences faculty are engaged in active research with students, classroom and clinical teaching through the on-campus Van Riper Language, Speech, and Hearing Clinics, and service to the university and professions. The Department is accredited by the Council on Academic Accreditation in Audiology and Speech-Language Pathology ( CAA ) of the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association ( ASHA ). Opportunities exist for interprofessional collaborations within the College, across the University, and with the Western Michigan University School of Medicine. Salary: Competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, with an excellent benefits package. Expected Start Date : January 1, 2027 Application Deadline : Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026 and continue until position is filled Required application documents: Faculty Credential Summary; CV; a letter describing qualifications, accomplishments, and professional experiences related to the position; and names, titles, postal and e-mail addresses, and telephone numbers of three references. Chair of Search committee: Kathy Rigley, M.A. WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Minorities, women, veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Major Duties Clinical supervision and mentorship of undergraduate and/or graduate students. Classroom teaching in the undergraduate and graduate programs in Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences. Interprofessional and intra-professional collaboration. Professional service to department, college, university, and/or profession. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in speech-language pathology from an accredited institution. Eligible for Michigan licensure for Speech-Language Pathology. Certificate of Clinical Competence from ASHA ( CCC - SLP ). 9 months of practice experience as a speech-language pathologist post certification. Completion of 2 hours of professional development in the area of supervision and/or clinical instruction prior to start date. Desired Qualifications Expertise in pediatric speech-language pathology. Experience in working with Deaf and hard of hearing clients and their families across communication modalities, including ASL and spoken language approaches. Experience supporting principles of diversity, equity, inclusion, and belonging in clinical practice. Experience with university teaching through in-person and virtual platforms. Experience with program coordination. Evidence of interprofessional and intra-professional collaboration. Knowledge and experience implementing evidence-based practice. At least 2 years of experience in clinical education/supervision. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Position Information Go to: wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Other Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5708": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I - Lecturer - Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering - Terminal 1/Year Appointment",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I - Lecturer - Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering - Terminal 1/Year Appointment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I - Lecturer - Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering - Terminal 1/Year Appointment Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Engineering/App Sci Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Mechanical & Aerospace Engr Posting Detail Information Posting Number F335P Job Type Non-Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade FS1 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Main Campus Salary Range Pay is commensurate with qualifications and experience, combined with an excellent benefits package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering at Western Michigan University invites applications for a full-time Faculty Specialist position. This is a teaching-focused position designed for a practitioner and educator who is dedicated to undergraduate instruction and student success. We are seeking candidates to fill two specific but overlapping needs within the department: Aerospace Engineering Focus: Primarily responsible for teaching undergraduate courses within the Aerospace Engineering curriculum. Mechanical Engineering Focus: Primarily responsible for teaching undergraduate courses within the Mechanical Engineering curriculum. Major Duties Teaching a full load of undergraduate courses, laboratories, and recitations in their respective discipline (Mechanical or Aerospace Engineering). Developing and updating course materials to ensure curriculum remains current with industry standards and accreditation requirements. Mentoring and advising undergraduate students, including the supervision of Senior Design projects. Maintaining and managing instructional laboratories and equipment. Participating in departmental, college, and university service committees. Collaborating with faculty to support student recruitment and retention efforts. Opportunity to participate in collaborative research activities in the department and college, though they are not required to develop an independent research program. Minimum Qualifications An earned Master of Science degree from an accredited institution in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a closely related discipline, AND a minimum of five (5) years of relevant professional expertise. OR an earned Ph.D. (or equivalent) from an accredited institution in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong oral and written communication skills. Desired Qualifications Demonstrated experience in teaching at the university level. Significant industrial experience in mechanical or aerospace design, manufacturing, or analysis. Experience with industry-standard engineering software and tools (e.g., CAD , FEA , CFD , etc.). A track record of effective mentorship or supervision of student projects. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Position Information Western Michigan University offers generous benefits to its employees including health, dental, vision, life and disability insurance, retirement, and tuition discount for the employee and tuition remission for eligible dependents. To access information about the specific benefits available for this position, go to: https://wmich.edu/hr/benefits-faculty The Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering offers ABET -accredited undergraduate programs in Mechanical Engineering and Aerospace Engineering, as well as Master’s and Ph.D. programs in both disciplines. Our faculty are dedicated to excellence in teaching and research, preparing students for successful careers in industry, government, and academia. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Other Teaching Philosophy Samples of Teaching Materials Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5691": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer- Physical Therapy - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer- Physical Therapy - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer- Physical Therapy - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Health & Human Svcs Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Physical Therapy Posting Detail Information Posting Number F337P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade I30/I20 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - East Campus Salary Range Pay is commensurate with qualifications and experience, combined with an excellent benefits package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary Western Michigan University invites applications for a full-time fiscal year, 12-month Tenure Track Faculty Specialist position in the Department of Physical Therapy. The ideal start date is July 1, 2026, and is flexible. The Department of Physical Therapy and the Doctor of Physical Therapy Program were established and approved in 2015. The Doctor of Physical Therapy Program at WMU achieved initial accreditation in December 2021 and will seek reaffirmation of accreditation in 2026. We are seeking highly motivated, energetic, and team-oriented individuals with demonstrated contemporary expertise in the following: Orthopedic physical therapy, advanced manual therapy, dry needling, biomechanics, kinesiology, and motor control. This individual will join a DPT faculty of eight (8) in growing and assessing a contemporary, innovative, and student-centered 2.5-year DPT program. Major Duties Experience working with students and colleagues from diverse communities, backgrounds, identities, learning styles, and abilities. Experience working with orthopedic populations across the lifespan and skilled in the management of individuals with musculoskeletal conditions. Teach in areas of expertise and additional assigned content areas. Supervise and advise students. Develop and sustain a scholarly research agenda in accordance with contemporary CAPTE standards and WMU institutional expectations. Provide service to the DPT program, department, university, profession, and community. Contribute to an interprofessional environment of instruction and community collaborations. Contribute to curricular and programmatic development and assessment. Participate in the accreditation process. Minimum Qualifications Earned Physical Therapy (PT) degree from an accredited institution, AND Academic credentials to include any of the following: PT degree AND an academic doctoral degree from an accredited institution (PhD, ScD, EdD, or DHSc), OR Clinical doctorate in physical therapy from an accredited institution ( DPT ) AND ABPTS certification. Evidence of physical therapy licensure, and eligibility/intention to obtain Michigan physical therapy licensure with the expectation for ongoing engagement in clinical practice and/or clinical research. 5 years demonstrated teaching and assessment experience (must be completed by date employment would commence). 1 year of experience teaching in a Doctor of Physical Therapy Program. Contemporary expertise in one or more of the identified areas of physical therapy. Experience with research and evidence of scholarly products. Strong oral, written, and interpersonal skills. Ability to function well within a collegial, collaborative work environment. Experience with CAPTE accreditation process. Membership in the American Physical Therapy Association. Desired Qualifications Academic doctoral degree (PhD, ScD, EdD, or DHSc) from an accredited institution. Completion of ABPTRFE accredited fellowship or residence. Completion of ABPTS certification. Demonstrated experience conducting research with a scholarly agenda that includes: History of external grant award/s for scientific research Evidence of disseminated products. National and/or international level presentation/s. Peer-reviewed publication/s. History of mentoring junior faculty in research. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Position Information Go to: wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5642": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - English - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor - English - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Assistant/Associate Professor - English - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications: Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The following documents will need to be submitted: Curriculum vita, including list of references Letter of application addressing minimum and desired qualifications Writing sample (no more than 30 pages) Statement of teaching philosophy Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Arts And Sciences Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department English Posting Detail Information Posting Number F332P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade I30/I20 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Main Campus Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Generous benefit package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary The Department of English at Western Michigan University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position at either the Assistant Professor or Associate Professor rank in Creative Writing (Fiction). This is an academic-year position, with the possibility of Summer instructional assignments for additional compensation. Major Duties The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active publishing agenda in fiction; provide effective instruction and mentoring to undergraduate and graduate students across creative writing and literature courses; support the success of a diverse population of undergraduate and graduate students; develop new curricula and course offerings; and contribute to department, college, and university service. Minimum Qualifications An M.F.A. or Ph.D. in Creative Writing or a closely related area, awarded by August 15, 2027. An original book-length work of fiction published by a reputable commercial, academic, or independent press. A record of effective teaching in creative writing at the undergraduate level. Desired Qualifications Creative productivity in a speculative fiction genre such as science fiction, climate fiction, fabulist fiction, or fantasy, as demonstrated by publication of an original book-length work by a reputable commercial, academic, or independent press; and/or record of multiple speculative fiction publications in peer-reviewed journals or magazines. A record of effective teaching in creative writing and literature courses, including in one or more speculative fiction areas, at the undergraduate and graduate levels. An established capacity for leadership in projects, programs, or partnerships, whether internal or external to the university. A demonstrated commitment to advancing equity across the areas of research and creative scholarship, teaching, and service. A documented history of promoting student engagement, success, and achievement. Special Instructions to Applicants Applications: Review of applications will begin on November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The following documents will need to be submitted: Curriculum vita, including list of references Letter of application addressing minimum and desired qualifications Writing sample (no more than 30 pages) Statement of teaching philosophy Additional Position Information Department: One of the largest units in Western Michigan University’s College of Arts and Sciences, the Department of English consists of 20 board-appointed, full-time faculty members. The department enrolls over 250 undergraduate majors and minors in creative writing, literature and language, and rhetoric and writing studies, and over 50 graduate students in master’s and doctoral programs in creative writing and literature and language. It is also home to the Gwen Frostic Reading Series and Third Coast Magazine. The College: Housing 23 academic departments, schools, and institutes that enroll nearly 3,000 undergraduate students and 700 graduate students, the College of Arts and Sciences represents the foundation of learning and the academic heart of WMU . The College is committed to fostering a community of diverse, inclusive, equitable, and globally engaged scholars, learners, and leaders, and it seeks candidates who can contribute to the College’s distinctive educational objectives, which promote interdisciplinary perspectives, intercultural understanding, and concern with social responsibility and the ethical implications of knowledge and action. University: Western Michigan University ( WMU ), located in Southwest Michigan, is a vibrant, nationally recognized student-centered research institution with an enrollment of 18,000. WMU delivers high-quality undergraduate instruction, has a strong graduate division, and fosters significant research activities. The Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching classifies WMU as a doctoral university and one of just 185 public universities in the nation conducting research at a high level. WMU recently received a $550 million endowed, multi-year Empowering Futures Gift, which will fund many projects and initiatives that aim to break down the barriers created by historic inequities. Kalamazoo: Kalamazoo is located only two and a half hours by car or train from Chicago and Detroit and only 45 minutes from the beaches of Lake Michigan. It occupies one of Michigan’s designated research corridors, maintaining a strong life sciences/biotech presence and supporting two leading medical centers. With 263,000 people in the greater Kalamazoo area, the community offers an array of cultural events, entertainment, and all-season recreation. The city supports a nationally recognized symphony and enjoys a vibrant community theatre and visual arts scene. Kalamazoo is dedicated to social justice, community development, and the elimination of generational poverty. The city is also home to the Kalamazoo Promise, a scholarship program offered to all Kalamazoo Public School students that covers up to 100% of tuition and fees to all Michigan public (and many private) institutions of higher learning. Compensation: Competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, with an excellent benefits package. Opportunities exist to teach in summer for additional compensation. Starting Date: August 15, 2027. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Writing Sample Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5500": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I / Faculty Specialist II - Aviation Specialist - College of Aviation - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I / Faculty Specialist II - Aviation Specialist - College of Aviation - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I / Faculty Specialist II - Aviation Specialist - College of Aviation - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For Other documents, please submit copies of front and back of all FAA certificates. Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Aviation Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department College of Aviation Posting Detail Information Posting Number F327P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade FS1/FS2 Campus Location WMU-Battle Creek - College of Aviation Salary Range Pay is commensurate with qualifications and experience, combined with an excellent benefits package. Number of Vacancies 2 General Summary The College of Aviation at Western Michigan University invites applications for a fiscal year, tenure-track flight faculty position. As an Aviation Specialist-Lead Flight Instructor, applicants will have the opportunity to teach the next generation of pilots in state-of-the-art airplanes. Applicants will join a supportive and collegial environment that values collaboration among students, faculty, and staff. This position represents an exceptional opportunity to contribute to a dynamic academic community and to bring professional flight experience into the airplane to enhance student learning. Major Duties Serve as a full-time flight instructor, providing flight, simulation, and ground instruction to assigned/scheduled aviation flight students. Assist with the training, standardization and mentoring of assigned temporary flight instructors. Assist the assigned Chief Flight Instructor as needed/directed. Assist the Student Progress Specialist in monitoring student progress. Maintain accurate, timely records/reports regarding student progress. Support the diverse curricula by maintaining the appropriate qualifications, proficiencies, and certificates to comply with governmental, organizational and accreditation requirements. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. FAA commercial pilot or airline transport pilot certificate with airplane SEL , MEL , and Instrument ratings. Second-class FAA medical certificate with at least third-class privileges. Unexpired FAA Flight Instructor certificate with airplane single-engine and instrument ratings. Desired Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited institution. Airline, military/governmental, charter, or corporate flight experience as PIC or SIC . Multi-engine instructor rating Collegiate FAR Part 141 aviation teaching experience. Other FAA Certificate (Dispatch, A&P, etc.) Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Special Instructions to Applicants For Other documents, please submit copies of front and back of all FAA certificates. Additional Position Information WMU’s College of Aviation has a storied 85-year history. With three distinct programs in flight, maintenance, and management, the College attracts students and faculty from all over the world. As a world-renowned program with one of the most modern fleets in collegiate aviation, WMU seeks to expand its students’ aviation opportunities. The College of Aviation offers its employees generous educational benefits, opportunities to train the next generation of aviators, and an excellent quality of life. There are multiple openings for this position. By applying to this posting, applicants will be considered for each position. Applicants may receive multiple email communications. Western Michigan University offers generous benefits to its employees including health, dental, vision, life and disability insurance, retirement, and tuition discount for the employee and tuition remission for eligible dependents. To access information about the specific benefits available for this position, go to: https://wmich.edu/hr/enrollment-faculty . Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Optional Documents Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5183": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Industrial and Entrepreneurial Engineering and Engineering Management - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Assistant Professor - Industrial and Entrepreneurial Engineering and Engineering Management - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Assistant Professor - Industrial and Entrepreneurial Engineering and Engineering Management - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Engineering/App Sci Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Indust & Entrep Eng & Eng Mgmt Posting Detail Information Posting Number F306P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade I30 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Parkview Campus Salary Range Pay is commensurate with qualifications and experience, combined with an excellent benefits package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary Western Michigan University has a position opening for a permanent full-time tenure track Assistant Professor in the Department of Industrial and Entrepreneurial Engineering and Engineering Management in Kalamazoo, MI starting August 15, 2026. Position requires a Doctor of Philosophy degree in Industrial Engineering or Engineering Management. Position also requires a Ph.D. dissertation in area of biomechanical modeling, and two peer-reviewed research publications in the field of industrial engineering and area of bio-mechanics. Major Duties Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Industrial Engineering & Engineering Management including Ergonomics & Occupational Bio-mechanics ( IEE 6420); Work Analysis (EM 3050); Work Analysis/Design Lab (EM 3150); Work Design ( IEE 2050); Ergonomics and Design ( IEE 3420). Advise graduate students. Conduct research in Industrial Engineering with a focus on biomechanical modeling. Publish results of research in peer-reviewed journals and present results at conferences. Attend committee and professional organization meetings. Minimum Qualifications Must have a Ph.D. dissertation in area of biomechanical modeling from an accredited institution. Two peer reviewed research publications in the field of industrial Engineering in the area of bio- mechanics. Desired Qualifications Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Position Information Go to: wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Other Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
