    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5983": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer - Mathematics - Terminal",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer - Mathematics - Terminal Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I/II - Lecturer - Mathematics - Terminal Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The following documents will need to be submitted: Cover letter that includes an explanation of how the candidate meets each of the minimal qualifications. Refer to submitted documents where evidence can be found (CV, transcript, etc.). for each desired qualification, a paragraph of one to five sentences describing how the candidate meets the qualification, or a statement that they do not. Refer to submitted documents for support. Curriculum vita. Evidence of teaching effectiveness. Teaching statement of no more than two pages that addresses your approach to teaching students from all backgrounds in service courses. Leadership statement of no more than two pages that addresses your vision for leading a multi-section course, including your approach to instructional quality, faculty development, assessment, collaboration with graduate students and adjunct instructors, and continuous course improvement. Contact information for three references. Unofficial or official copy of graduate transcript. One sample of an activity or assessment written or significantly revised by the candidate with a description of your contribution to the current form of the activity or assessment. Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Arts And Sciences Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Mathematics Posting Detail Information Posting Number F360P Job Type Non-Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade FS1/FS2 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Main Campus Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Generous benefit package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary The Department of Mathematics at Western Michigan University invites applications for a 1.5 year, terminal, full-time position at the Faculty Specialist I or II rank in Mathematics with the potential for renewal. This is an alternate academic-year position, with the possibility of summer instructional assignment for additional compensation. The anticipated start date is January 1, 2027 and the end date is May 14, 2028. Review of applications will begin October 19, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Major Duties Contribute to the teaching and service missions of WMU . Provide effective mathematics instruction to undergraduate students in service courses. Support the success of the diverse populations of undergraduate students, including adjusting offerings for the changing backgrounds of students and the needs of client disciplines. Lead teams of instructors (including graduate students and adjunct instructors) in multi-section courses, including schedule, syllabus, course objectives, assessments, and professional development. Contribute to department, college, and university committees. Minimum Qualifications A master’s or doctoral degree in applied mathematics, mathematics, mathematics education, or a closely related field from an accredited institution awarded by the end of 2026. Academic preparation to teach introductory and intermediate undergraduate mathematics courses, including calculus, multivariable calculus, and differential equations. Two years undergraduate teaching in mathematics or a closely related field. Experience working with multiple instructors on a common course. Experience with online learning-management systems. Desired Qualifications Evidence of successful and innovative mathematics teaching. Established capacity to serve as lead coordinator for multi-section courses. This includes providing course-specific professional development, mentoring and supervision for new instructors. Demonstrated ability to teach classes that provide technical skills for students enrolled in non- STEM majors, such as MATH 1140 and 1160 at WMU . Demonstrated ability to teach classes that improve the pre-algebra and algebra skills of students to prepare them for the math courses and content required for their majors and careers ( MATH 1090, 1100, and 1110 at WMU ). Ability to serve as support or lead the coordination of other multi-section courses if the need arises, including precalculus, calculus sequence, and linear algebra ( MATH 1178, 1179, 1180, 1220, 1230, 2300, 2720, 3740) or mathematics education ( MATH 1520, 2530, 2530, and 3550). A documented history of promoting student engagement, success, and achievement. An exhibited ability to implement AI or other technologies in the classroom. Special Instructions to Applicants The following documents will need to be submitted: Cover letter that includes an explanation of how the candidate meets each of the minimal qualifications. Refer to submitted documents where evidence can be found (CV, transcript, etc.). for each desired qualification, a paragraph of one to five sentences describing how the candidate meets the qualification, or a statement that they do not. Refer to submitted documents for support. Curriculum vita. Evidence of teaching effectiveness. Teaching statement of no more than two pages that addresses your approach to teaching students from all backgrounds in service courses. Leadership statement of no more than two pages that addresses your vision for leading a multi-section course, including your approach to instructional quality, faculty development, assessment, collaboration with graduate students and adjunct instructors, and continuous course improvement. Contact information for three references. Unofficial or official copy of graduate transcript. One sample of an activity or assessment written or significantly revised by the candidate with a description of your contribution to the current form of the activity or assessment. Additional Position Information Visit wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy Samples of Teaching Materials Other Transcripts List of References Optional Documents Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5982": {
      "title": "Faculty Specialist I - Clinical Specialist - Counselor Education and Counseling Psychology - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Faculty Specialist I - Clinical Specialist - Counselor Education and Counseling Psychology - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Faculty Specialist I - Clinical Specialist - Counselor Education and Counseling Psychology - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Educ & Human Dvlpmt Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Counselor Educ/Counselng Psych Posting Detail Information Posting Number F352P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade FS1 Campus Location WMU-Grand Rapids - Downtown Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Generous benefit package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary The Department of Counselor Education and Counseling Psychology is seeking a faculty specialist I with specialization in Counseling Psychology. Major Duties Serving as Director of the Center for Counseling and Psychological Services in Grand Rapids ( CCPS -GR) for Counseling Psychology (6 credit hour assignment). Advising master’s students in Counseling Psychology (CP), serving on CP doctoral student committees as second member, and participating in faculty committee work and professional service at the department or college level (3 credit hour assignment). Teaching equivalent of 6 credit hours of graduate courses (each fall and spring) in our APA -accredited Counseling Psychology doctoral program and master’s level courses in Counseling Psychology. Potential for fulfilling the clinical coordination in Counseling Psychology role for equivalent of one 3 credit hour reassignment. Providing administrative guidance for daily center operations and overseeing all activities taking place in CCPS -GR and direct supervision for clinic personnel (i.e., Administrative Assistant, doctoral graduate assistants and student front desk workers). Coordination and supervision of intake procedures within CCPS -GR. Maintaining CCPS -GR training materials, overseeing orientations each semester, and providing ongoing support to instructors and students. Coordinating and providing clinical supervision for master’s and doctoral level students. Securing client referrals, marketing center services (with support of CEHD marketing team) and establishing and maintaining relationships with community partners to support the CCPS -GR training mission. Seeking service contracts and/or grants that can be used to support the training mission of the CCPS -GR. Overseeing operational budget for the CCPS -GR (e.g., maintaining a sliding fee scale for clients, managing expenses, supplies). Work with technology utilized in the CCPS -GR in support of clinical experiences and courses as well as the training of students and staff. Other duties as assigned by the department chair. Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate in Counseling Psychology from an accredited institution with degree completion before contract start date, with preference for graduates of an APA accredited Counseling Psychology doctoral program. Eligibility for licensure as a doctoral level psychologist (Licensed Psychologist) in Michigan before contract start date. Ability to contribute to advancing the Counseling Psychology program’s and training clinic’s emphasis on race and other issues of diversity. Readiness to provide clinical supervision. Ability to teach counseling psychology doctoral courses and foundational master’s courses in counseling psychology while infusing race and other issues of diversity. The willingness to contribute to the Counseling Psychology Training Committee ( CPTC ) and engage in activities commensurate with a Counseling Psychology professional identity. Desired Qualifications Experience teaching or desire to teach applied or practice focused courses. Past experience serving as a clinical supervisor. Willingness to work on building relationships and engagements with community agencies and traditionally underserved populations. Interest or experience using advanced instructional technologies to improve the teaching/learning process. Overseeing training and psychological testing by doctoral graduate associates, if desired. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Position Information For benefits and other information visit https://wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty . Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Other Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5981": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Communication - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor - Communication - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Assistant/Associate Professor - Communication - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should visit http://www.wmich.edu/hr/jobs to apply. Online applications include: 1. Curriculum vita. 2. Letter of application that addresses fulfillment of qualifications and demonstrates skills and knowledge consistent with the position requirements. 3. Representative examples of convention and/or published research. 4. Three samples of teaching materials (e.g., syllabi, assignments, prepared materials for class). 5. Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts. Please direct any questions to Andrew Bryant (andrew.d.bryant@wmich.edu). Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Arts And Sciences Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Communication Posting Detail Information Posting Number F359P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade I30/I20 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Main Campus Salary Range Pay is commensurate with qualifications and experience, combined with an excellent benefits package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary Position Summary The School of Communication at Western Michigan University invites applications for a full-time tenure track position in Organizational/Strategic Communication at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, to begin August 2027. Faculty will contribute to a dynamic program in organizational/strategic communication situated within a liberal arts curriculum, emphasizing critical thinking to inform student work. The candidate should have experience with (or interest in) the operation and growth of internship programs and other professional field experiences for undergraduates. The instructional load for this position includes administrative and teaching responsibilities related to the internship program, which accounts for a substantial part of the instructional workload. Responsibilities Candidates will teach organizational or strategic communication courses in their area(s) of expertise, direct an internship program, and maintain a nationally recognized research agenda. The ability to teach foundational courses also is expected. Major Duties Teach organizational or strategic communication courses. Direct the School’s internship program. Maintain nationally recognized research agenda. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Participate in departmental and college service. Engage in curriculum development. Develop experiential learning opportunities. Integrate inclusivity and equity into scholarship, teaching, service, and student mentoring. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in organizational or strategic communication from an accredited institution. (ABDs are eligible for consideration but are required to complete their degree requirements by August 5, 2027.) Experience with the operation and growth of internship programs or other professional field experiences for undergraduates. Demonstrated strong potential for nationally recognized program of research. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching. Desired Qualifications Ability to develop community partnerships to advance students’ professional development. Experience with experiential learning and/or student-faculty research collaborations. Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should visit http://www.wmich.edu/hr/jobs to apply. Online applications include: 1. Curriculum vita. 2. Letter of application that addresses fulfillment of qualifications and demonstrates skills and knowledge consistent with the position requirements. 3. Representative examples of convention and/or published research. 4. Three samples of teaching materials (e.g., syllabi, assignments, prepared materials for class). 5. Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts. Please direct any questions to Andrew Bryant (andrew.d.bryant@wmich.edu). Additional Position Information Go to: wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. University We would like to recognize that Western Michigan University is located on lands historically occupied by Ojibwe, Odawa, and Bodewadmi nations. WMU seeks to acknowledge and honor this ancestral land of the Three Fires Confederacy, the sacred lands of all indigenous peoples and their continued presence. Western Michigan University ( WMU ), located in Southwest Michigan, is a vibrant, nationally recognized student-centered research institution with an enrollment of nearly 18,000. WMU delivers high-quality undergraduate instruction, has a strong graduate division, and fosters significant research activities. The Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching has placed WMU among the 185 public institutions in the nation designated as research universities with high research activities. Western Michigan University is a globally engaged university that promotes success for learners at all levels and stands out among America’s more than 4,600 public and private degree-granting colleges and universities. WMU is committed to our motto, “So That All May Learn,” and to creating an inclusive environment and equitable structures for hiring, teaching, learning and research. Several years ago, the university received a $550 million Empowering Futures Gift, which funds many projects and initiatives that aim to break down the barriers created by historic inequities. At the time it was received, the Empowering Futures Gift was the largest gift for a public institution of higher education in U.S. history. Annual employment surveys show that upon graduation, 9 of 10 WMU graduates are employed, with 94% landing positions related to their degree. Military Times has recognized WMU among its best institutions for veterans each survey year since 2010. WMU operates the nation’s largest and most comprehensive collegiate support program for former foster-care youth. Department The School of Communication at Western Michigan University embraces the philosophy of engaged scholarship – a philosophy that grounds our theory and research in a practical effort to make an impact on our personal relationships, organizations, communities, society, and the global community. We have a nationally recognized master’s program and 17 tenured/tenure-track faculty who have national and international research and creative activity records and who are actively engaged in student mentoring. Our graduate program engages students in public scholarship, providing transparent criteria for student success, and employs the best practices such as teamwork, interdisciplinary approaches, and mentoring. Our undergraduate curriculum serves approximately 300 students in six majors, including Communication Studies; Digital Media and Journalism; Film, Video, and Media Studies; Interpersonal Communication; Public Relations and Social Media Strategy; and Strategic Communication, and 200 students in four minors: Communication, User-Experience/ Human-Computer Interaction (UX/ HCI ), Film and Digital Storytelling, and Journalism. This position coincides with a multi-million-dollar renovation of Dunbar Hall, which includes a highly visible broadcast production space ideal for live news and sports shows, interviews with visiting scholars, professionals, or alumni, chroma key, photography shoots, or other performance-based activities. The School of Communication is committed to the University’s strategic direction on inclusive excellence and equity and actively works to promote a welcoming, equitable, and inclusive University culture to ensure social sustainability and accessibility. We strongly encourage applications from all qualified candidates, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. We seek all candidates who have a passion for accessibility and working with all students. In support of the School of Communication’s commitment to scholarly and creative activity, the successful candidate will enjoy many opportunities to develop their research and/or production activity portfolio. Travel funding will be provided, with support for presenting at conferences, publishing in professional publications, creative activities, and developing leadership experience. College The College of Arts and Sciences represents the foundation of learning and the academic heart of WMU . As articulated in the College of Arts and Sciences strategic plan, we are committed to fostering a community of globally engaged scholars, learners, and leaders. With 22 departments and interdisciplinary schools and institutes, WMU’s largest college offers a broad range of learning opportunities and career paths for our students. CAS students are among the very top students in the country, having received very competitive awards including Goldwater Fellowships, Udall Scholarships, Boren Fellowships, and Fulbright awards, among others. Kalamazoo Kalamazoo is located only two and a half hours by car from Chicago and Detroit and only 45 minutes from the beaches of Lake Michigan. It is in one of Michigan’s designated research corridors, maintaining a strong life sciences/biotech presence and supporting two leading medical centers. With 263,000 people in the greater Kalamazoo area, the community offers an array of cultural events, entertainment, and all-season recreation. The city supports an international keyboard competition and a nationally recognized symphony and has earned a reputation for a vibrant community theatre and visual arts scene. Relatedly, Kalamazoo is committed to social justice, community development and the elimination of generational poverty through its Shared Prosperity Kalamazoo initiative, with structural budgetary support provided by the City of Kalamazoo’s Foundation for Excellence program. Kalamazoo also is the home of the Kalamazoo Promise, a scholarship program offered to all Kalamazoo Public School students that covers up to 100% of tuition and mandatory fees to all Michigan public (and many private) institutions of higher learning. Compensation Competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, with an excellent benefits package, including participation in TIAA . Opportunities exist to teach in the summer for additional compensation. Starting Date August 2027 Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Samples of Teaching Materials Writing Sample Optional Documents Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.wmujobs.org/postings/5978": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Educational Leadership, Research and Technology - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Western Michigan University Portal | Assistant Professor - Educational Leadership, Research and Technology - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Virtual Visit Kalamazoo Promise Office of Institutional Equity Diversity and Inclusion Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs Assistant Professor - Educational Leadership, Research and Technology - Tenure Track Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Summary College College Of Educ & Human Dvlpmt Executive Area Provost & VP Academic Affairs Department Educational Leadership, Research and Technology Posting Detail Information Posting Number F361P Job Type Tenure Track Pay Type Exempt/Salaried Pay Grade I30 Campus Location WMU-Kalamazoo - Main Campus Salary Range Commensurate with experience. Generous benefit package. Number of Vacancies 1 General Summary Western Michigan University’s College of Education and Human Development invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Organizational Change Leadership. The individual in this position will serve in the Organizational Change Leadership ( OCL ) unit within the Department of Educational Leadership, Research, and Technology at Western Michigan University ( WMU ). The OCL unit is comprised of a suite of academic programs that includes a PHD in Organizational Change Leadership, an MA in Organizational Change Leadership, a Graduate Certificate in Organizational Change Leadership, and an Undergraduate Minor in Organizational Change Leadership. We seek to hire someone who can fill needed content expertise areas (organizational development, organizational culture, power and politics, and applied change leadership), and provide new energy and perspectives related to teaching; recruiting, retaining, and advising students; and research. This individual will also serve on committees for doctoral students in the PhD in Organizational Change Leadership. To attain and keep graduate faculty status (which is required to teach in a graduate program at the institution), this individual will be required to maintain an active research agenda. Ideally, this faculty member should have connections with thought leaders in the profession, as well as in professional associations in the field of organizational development and change. The individual in this position will also be expected to teach courses, maintain office hours, and support program initiatives on campus, in-person in Kalamazoo, Michigan. Major Duties Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Organizational Change Leadership beginning in August 2027, with primary responsibility for high-quality online instruction. Maintain an active research agenda in organizational development and change and contribute meaningfully to the advancement of the field. Advise and mentor students across the OCL undergraduate minor, graduate certificate, master’s, and doctoral programs. Recruit and engage prospective students and contribute to the continued growth and visibility of the OCL programs. Contribute to curriculum innovation, course development, and continuous improvement across OCL programs. Contribute actively to the intellectual and professional life of the OCL unit and provide service to the department, college, and university. Maintain a visible presence in the organizational development and change scholarly community through conference presentations, publications, professional service, and disciplinary leadership. Engage actively in relevant professional associations, particularly the Organization Development and Change ( ODC ) and Management Consulting (MC) Divisions of the Academy of Management. Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in Organizational Development and Change, Organizational Behavior, Organization Studies, Industrial-Organizational Psychology, Organizational Psychology, Organizational and Social Psychology, or Human and Organizational Studies, with a substantive emphasis on organizational development, conferred by the start of a Fall 2027 appointment from an accredited institution. An emerging research agenda and record of peer-reviewed publications and/or presentations appropriate for career stage in organizational development and change, organizational behavior, or organizational studies. Demonstrated professional and/or scholarly engagement in organizational development and change through participation in professional associations, conferences, scholarly networks, and/or professional practice. Demonstrated experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses in one or more of the following areas: organizational development, organizational change, organizational diagnosis, leadership, group dynamics, organizational power and politics, organizational culture, or closely related areas of organizational studies. Experience with, or demonstrated ability to develop, high-quality online instruction. Commitment to working with a broad range of students and mentoring adult learners from varied professional, organizational, and educational backgrounds. Desired Qualifications Substantive organizational consulting or change leadership experience across settings such as business and industry, nonprofit organizations, healthcare, government, or the military. Demonstrated ability to translate organizational development and change theory and research into professional practice. Expertise in quantitative, qualitative, and/or mixed-methods research. Experience advising and mentoring undergraduate, master’s, and/or doctoral students, including service on dissertation committees. Demonstrated expertise in curriculum development and the design of innovative courses and learning experiences for working professionals. Evidence of leadership in professional, academic, and/or organizational settings. Experience or interest in developing partnerships with organizations, professional associations, or other external constituencies that support teaching, research, or student opportunities. Special Instructions to Applicants Additional Position Information Go to: wmich.edu/hr/employees/faculty for benefits and other information. Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Other Contact Us Human Resources Western Michigan University 1903 W Michigan Ave Kalamazoo, MI 49008 Phone (269) 387-3620 Fax (269) 387-3441 WMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. Protected veterans, individuals with disabilities and all other qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
  },
